      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): bound conflict-marker scan reads to prevent OOM on large files",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`pnpm check:no-conflict-markers` previously read every candidate tracked file returned by `git grep` into memory whole via `fs.readFileSync`. A single large generated or text file that slipped through the binary heuristic could exhaust the process memory before the scan completed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Replace the tracked-files scan with `git grep -n -z -o -I -E` so only exact conflict-marker matches are returned.\n- Parse the grep output (path, line number, match) into violation records without buffering file contents.\n- Parse the NUL-delimited pathname before any newline-based record splitting so tracked filenames containing newlines are reported intact.\n- Keep `findConflictMarkersInFiles` for direct, small-scale use; the tracked-files path no longer reads files whole.\n- `findConflictMarkersInTrackedFiles` now returns paths relative to the repository root, matching `git grep` output.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Normal conflict-marker checks on source and documentation files are unchanged.\n- Oversized or generated files can no longer cause an OOM during the scan because their contents are never read.\n- CI and pre-commit runs remain robust against accidental large-file commits.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal focused test passes:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.test.ts --run\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\n✓ |tooling| test/scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.test.ts (10 tests) 633ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\nTerminal proof on head `b8657525ff2` against a fixture git repo containing a tracked 61 MiB file (over the previous 50 MiB scan cap) with conflict markers near the end, plus a tracked file whose name contains a newline:\n\n```\n$ du -h generated/oversized.txt\n61M\tgenerated/oversized.txt\n\n$ node --max-old-space-size=128 scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.mjs\nFound unresolved merge conflict markers:\n- docs/weird\nname.md:2,4,6\n- generated/oversized.txt:6145,6147,6149\nexit=1 (violations reported) | peak RSS 66 MB | wall clock 0.24s\n```\n\nThe 61 MiB file is never read whole: the run completes in 0.24s with a 66 MB peak RSS under a 128 MB heap cap. The newline-containing path is preserved intact (`docs/weird\\nname.md:2,4,6`, printed across two terminal lines because the path itself contains the newline); the previous newline-first parser silently truncated it to `name.md`. A complementary clean fixture (61 MiB, no markers) exits 0 in 0.17s with a 65 MB peak RSS.\n\nAdded regression tests covering:\n- tracked files with conflict markers reported via `git grep`\n- clean tracked files returning no violations\n- binary tracked files skipped by `git grep -I`\n- paths containing spaces and unusual characters\n- tracked filenames containing newlines (NUL-delimited path parsed before record splitting)\n- large files whose line numbers are reported without reading the whole file\n- `main()` printing paths relative to the repository root\n\nRebased onto current `upstream/main` to pick up the independent `scripts/lib/sqlite-reliability-runner.ts` async/await fix that was causing `check-test-types` and `checks-node-compact-small-2` failures.",
        "branch": "fix/scripts-bound-conflict-marker-scan",
